      "name": "Location stream (WebSocket)",
      "item": [],
      "description": "Postman's collection format can't store WebSocket requests, so create it in the app:\n\n1. Run `Negotiate the location stream`; it saves Map's URL with a one-time ticket into {{wsUrl}}.\n2. New -> WebSocket, URL {{wsUrl}} (save it in this collection so the variable resolves), Connect within 60 s.\n3. Send { \"userId\": \"{{aliceId}}\", \"lat\": 47.02, \"lng\": 28.83, \"timestamp\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\" }\n4. Map acks: { \"event\": \"ack\", \"data\": { \"status\": \"updated\" } }\n\nA ticket opens one socket only. A reused or expired ticket, or a frame for another player, closes it with 1008."
